ts","fy":"2025/26"}],"calendar":{"upcoming":[{"date":"2026-09-23","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-19","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"New; Extraordinary Council","webcast":false,"url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-10","committee":"Audit, Governance & Standards Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-02","committee":"Finance & Future Development Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-12-09","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-07-08","committee":"Finance & Future Development Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-15","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-07-28","committee":"Audit, Governance & Standards Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Audit, Governance & Standards Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-17","committee":"Finance & Future Development Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Brentwood's capital spending plan falls 25% behind in first quarter, creating delivery risk","lead":"Brentwood council is on track to spend only three-quarters of its planned capital expenditure in the first quarter of 2026/27, with a \u00a313.6 million shortfall against a \u00a354.5 million budget. The underspend masks volatile performance across individual projects. The council's affordable housing programme, budgeted at \u00a337.2 million for the quarter, is forecast to spend only \u00a326.2 million, a 30 per cent slip. Meanwhile, the Baytree project is running at just 20 per cent of its planned \u00a35 million spend. However, two other major projects are overrunning: the Depot Redevelopment faces a \u00a31 million overspend and the Brentwood Centre Redevelopment a \u00a3591,000 overspend. The quarterly shortfall raises questions about whether the council can deliver its capital programme on schedule.","iso":"2026-09-17","paper_title":"2026/27 Q1 Budget Update","paper_url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s31410/31410.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Brentwood's capital spending falls \u00a313.6m short in first quarter","lead":"Brentwood Council underspent by \u00a313.6m on capital spending \u2014 money spent on things that last, such as buildings, roads, vehicles and equipment \u2014 in the first quarter, reaching only \u00a341m of its \u00a354.5m target. The shortfall masks mixed progress across individual projects. The Baytree scheme was just 20% spent at \u00a31m against a quarterly budget of \u00a35m, while the Affordable Housing programme fell 30% short of plan. Other schemes overran: the Depot Redevelopment more than doubled its quarterly budget, and the Brentwood Centre Redevelopment spent 42% more than budgeted. The council's Housing Revenue Account, funded by tenants' rents, also faces emerging pressure from disrepair compensation claims, pushing it towards a \u00a3510k deficit.","iso":"2026-09-17","paper_title":"2026/27 Q1 Budget Update","paper_url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s31410/31410.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Finance & Future Development Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 1 for 2026/27 Q1 Budget Update","paper_url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s31411/31411.pdf","headline":"Overall capital programme underspent by 25% in Q1, with (\u00a313,573k) variance","detail":"The total capital programme shows budgeted spend of \u00a354,548k against a Q1 forecast outturn of \u00a340,975k, a variance of (\u00a313,573k). The council is on track to spend only 75% of planned Q1 capital expenditure.","category":"capital","matters":"Capital programme delivery is a key indicator of project management and financial control; a 25% Q1 underspend raises whether the council will meet full-year capital expenditure targets and the implications for financing and cash flow forecasting.","figures":"Budgeted \u00a354,548k, Q1 forecast \u00a340,975k, variance (\u00a313,573k)","quote":"CAPPRO CAPITAL PROGRAMME 54,548 40,975 (13,573) 0","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Finance & Future Development Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 1 for 2026/27 Q1 Budget Update","paper_url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s31411/31411.pdf","headline":"HRA Affordable Housing programme shows 30% Q1 underspend with (\u00a311,018k) variance","detail":"The HRA Affordable Housing programme was budgeted at \u00a337,185k for Q1 but is forecast to spend only \u00a326,167k, a significant underspend of (\u00a311,018k) representing 30% of planned Q1 expenditure.","category":"capital","matters":"Affordable housing delivery is typically match-funded and subject to grant conditions; substantial underspend suggests delivery delays or programme changes that could affect grant certainty and the council's ability to meet housing commitments.","figures":"Budgeted \u00a337,185k, Q1 forecast \u00a326,167k, variance (\u00a311,018k)","quote":"CJB HRA Affordable Housing 37,185 26,167 (11,018)","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Finance & Future Development Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 1 for 2026/27 Q1 Budget Update","paper_url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s31411/31411.pdf","headline":"Brentwood Centre Redevelopment is overrunning, with \u00a3591k overspend against \u00a31,409k Q1 budget","detail":"The Brentwood Centre Redevelopment was budgeted at \u00a31,409k for Q1 but is forecast to spend \u00a32,000k, a \u00a3591k overspend representing a 42% cost overrun on planned Q1 spend.","category":"capital","matters":"Major council redevelopment projects showing cost overruns signal project delivery risk and create uncertainty around total project financing and the council's capital position.","figures":"Budgeted \u00a31,409k, Q1 forecast \u00a32,000k, overspend \u00a3591k","quote":"C239 Brentwood Centre Redevelopment 1,409 2,000 591","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Finance & Future Development Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 1 for 2026/27 Q1 Budget Update","paper_url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s31411/31411.pdf","headline":"Depot Redevelopment is overrunning at more than 100% of Q1 budget, with \u00a31,000k overspend","detail":"The Depot Redevelopment project was budgeted at \u00a3987k for Q1 but is forecast to spend \u00a31,987k, an overspend of \u00a31,000k. The forecast outturn has doubled the planned Q1 expenditure.","category":"capital","matters":"Cost overruns of this scale indicate potential cost control issues or scope drift that could affect the total project outturn and the council's overall capital position, with implications for borrowing requirements.","figures":"Budgeted \u00a3987k, Q1 forecast \u00a31,987k, overspend \u00a31,000k","quote":"C241 Depot Redevelopment 987 1,987 1,000","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-17","committee":"Finance & Future Development Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 1 for 2026/27 Q1 Budget Update","paper_url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s31411/31411.pdf","headline":"Baytree project is 80% underspent in Q1, with (\u00a33,979k) variance against \u00a34,979k budget","detail":"The Baytree capital project was budgeted at \u00a34,979k for Q1 but is forecast to spend only \u00a31,000k. This represents a variance of (\u00a33,979k), indicating either substantial project delay or delivery disruption.","category":"capital","matters":"A lender needs to understand whether capital projects are being delivered on schedule; an 80% underspend in Q1 suggests project delays, capability issues, or funding constraints that could affect the council's ability to spend planned capital and refinance accordingly.","figures":"Budgeted \u00a34,979k, Q1 forecast \u00a31,000k, variance (\u00a33,979k)","quote":"C228 Baytree 4,979 1,000 (3,979) 0","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-17"},"name":"Brentwood","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-23","since_iso":"2026-08-24","distress":false,"headline":"Overall capital programme underspent by 25% in Q1, with (\u00a313,573k) variance","lead":"Capital programme delivery is a key indicator of project management and financial control; a 25% Q1 underspend raises whether the council will meet full-year capital expenditure targets and the implications for financing and cash flow forecasting.","also":["33 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Audit, Governance & Standards Committee on 2026-11-10","n_findings":34,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix 1 for 2026/27 Q1 Budget Update","top_paper_url":"https://brentwood.moderngov.co.uk/documents/s31411/31411.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":93,"news_drafts_total":2}}